    "Accuracy intervals (Wilson) treat sessions as independent.",
    "Simulated returns assume a flat cost per trade, no slippage or taxes, and cash that earns no interest.",
    "Following always_up is buy-and-hold; it is the return benchmark.",
    "The base-rate Brier score uses the share of up days in the tested period, which no forecaster knew in advance, so it is a slightly hard reference."
  ]
}
